        <td class="NewsText" style="font-size: 15px">The <a href="alma">AlmaLinux</a> OS project has published updates to both its 10.x and 9.x branches. The two new versions were announced together: "<span class="Quote">The AlmaLinux OS Foundation is announcing the general availability of AlmaLinux OS 10.3, code-named 'Mauve Lion', and AlmaLinux OS 9.9 code-named 'Chartreuse Bobcat'. AlmaLinux 10.3 adds GCC Toolset 16, LLVM Toolset 22, Rust 1.97, Go 1.27, GDB 17.2 and Node.js 26. Security updates include fapolicyd 2.0, Keylime 7.14, audit 4.2 with post-quantum TLS for remote logging and libreswan 5.4 with ML-KEM post-quantum key exchange. ModSecurity is back - the mod_security web application firewall and the OWASP Core Rule Set (CRS) are back in AlmaLinux 10. They shipped in AlmaLinux 8 and 9 but were not included in 10.0 through 10.2. This release is a big version bump. AlmaLinux 9 ships ModSecurity 2.9.6 with CRS 3.3, and 10.3 ships ModSecurity 2.9.14 with CRS 4.22. CRS 4 reorganized the rule set, so if you’re bringing rules or tuning over from an AlmaLinux 9 server, plan to review them before you put 10.3 in front of production traffic.</span>" Additional details can be found in the <a href="https://almalinux.org/blog/2026-11-16-almalinux_103_and_99_stable/">release announcement</a>. <a href="https://almalinux.org/get-almalinux/">Download</a> (SHA256): <a href="https://repo.almalinux.org/almalinux/10/isos/x86_64/AlmaLinux-10.3-x86_64-dvd.iso">AlmaLinux-10.3-x86_64-dvd.iso</a> (10,323MB, <a href="https://repo.almalinux.org/almalinux/10.3/isos/x86_64/AlmaLinux-10.3-x86_64.torrent">torrent</a>, <a href="table.php?distribution=alma&amp;pkglist=true&amp;version=10.3#pkglist">pkglist</a>), <a href="https://repo.almalinux.org/almalinux/9/isos/x86_64/AlmaLinux-9.9-x86_64-dvd.iso">AlmaLinux-9.9-x86_64-dvd.iso</a> (15,159MB, <a href="https://repo.almalinux.org/almalinux/9.9/isos/x86_64/AlmaLinux-9.9-x86_64.torrent">torrent</a>).</td>
