        <td class="NewsText" style="font-size: 15px">Lime Technology, Inc. has announced the release of <a href="unraid">Unraid</a> OS 7.4.0, an updated version of the company's commercial Linux distribution designed for Network-Attached Storage (NAS) deployments. The new release updates the Linux kernel to version 6.18.60 and brings various improvements to its web-based administration user interface: "<span class="Quote">Unraid OS 7.4.0 is now available as the latest stable release. It adds multiple custom networks and memory limits for Docker containers, Mover progress tracking, improved file operations, a shared task tray, and new boot-device backup and power-button options. This release also includes WebGUI and Unraid API security fixes, updates the Linux kernel to 6.18.60, and updates base packages to address reported CVEs. Highlights: multiple Docker networks - container templates can now attach to more than one custom network, those attachments stay in place when a container is updated or recreated; docker memory limits - Docker Add/Edit forms include a memory limit field in Advanced View; mover progress - mover now tracks progress and status and it preserves hard links while moving files; shared task tray - manage background operations from one task tray, with live or completed output available from any browser tab....</span>" Continue to the <a href="https://unraid.net/blog/unraid-7-4-0">release announcement</a> to read the complete list of changes. <a href="https://docs.unraid.net/unraid-os/download_list/">Download (MD5)</a>: <a href="https://releases.unraid.net/dl/stable/7.4.0/5d32b11ee717f3bcc946145606b84cea85fc8cf6d0eb63c2b66649984b6817c7/unRAIDServer-7.4.0-x86_64.zip">unRAIDServer-7.4.0-x86_64.zip</a> (1,177MB).</td>
